From c037e46a4904915daac5137bcdefe2c6be6d7ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): optimize routed MoE dispatch scan, grouped GEMM
 sync, and empty-slab SwiGLU skip

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
In vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/moe.py:
1. _dispatch_macros.layout() previously computed the 512-thread per-expert padded route prefix sum via a 9-step Hillis-Steele shared-memory scan with 18 CTA-wide __syncthreads() barriers (25 total in fused moe_dispatch_v41). Replace the shared-memory scan with a two-level warp-shuffle prefix scan (__shfl_up_sync within each warp, a single shared-memory warp-total write and __syncthreads(), and an in-register warp-prefix scan via __shfl_up_sync + __shfl_sync), reducing CTA barriers in fused moe_dispatch_v41 from 25 to 7.
2. Enable TL_DISABLE_THREAD_STORAGE_SYNC and TL_DISABLE_SAFE_MEMORY_ACCESS across grouped_fp8_fp4_gemm, moe_swiglu_cast, moe_dispatch_v41, and moe_combine_v41; remove redundant ptx_commit_group() / ptx_wait_group(stages - 1) in grouped_fp8_fp4_gemm (since cp_async_barrier_noinc(loaded[s]) already tracks each stage's cp.async transactions); use __syncwarp() instead of __syncthreads() after SFB_shared scale expansion when block_M == 16 and sfb_copies == 1 (1-warp decode CTAs); and unify non-gather metadata preload (TileExpert, Order, SFBase, Narrow) before pdl.wait() / pdl.chain() with early exit before pdl.wait() on empty CTAs.
3. In moe_swiglu_cast, preserve rows_per_cta = 4 if warps >= 4 else 2, cascade Order and Weights preloads before pdl.chain() so empty slabs only read orders[0] and 1-row tiles only read orders[0..1] and weights[0], exit empty slabs immediately after pdl.chain() via if expert >= 0 and orders[0] >= 0:, and guard rows 1..rows_per_cta-1 behind if rows_per_cta > 1 and orders[1] >= 0:.

Quality:
Bit-identical (0 uint16 diffs, identical SHA-256 digests) across all TP4 (I=576) and TP3 (I=768) decode batch sizes M in 1..48, both eager and inside captured CUDA graphs (chain and cold-L2 + _l2pf_ffn modes). Across 2 fresh container boots (24 interleaved paired windows per cell on 6 serving DeepseekV4DecoderLayers), 25/26 TP4 cells and 22/26 TP3 cells have faster paired medians (30/52 cells statistically significantly faster by 95% bootstrap CI, 0/52 slower), saving up to -2.55 us/layer (+1.20%) at M=1, -5.29 us/layer at M=28, and -15.30 us/layer at M=48.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_moe.py tests/models/deepseek_v4_1/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py (139 passed across 2 fresh container boots).

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang MoE optimization for SM120/SM121.
